A||||13||84 2in1||PLEASE HELP cooling fan prob.||||1||
Z||000000||84 2in1||06-11-2001||05:40 PM||||my 84 has the hevy duty cooling fan with factory AC. the stupid thing will not come on at all! Replaced the switch in the head NOTHING! Turn on the AC NOTHING again! the fan is good but cannot make out the relays or the wireing. can any one give me some guidance here? PLEASE!?!?-B- ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ROB MAC||06-11-2001||05:59 PM||||There is a relay near the fan , a fuse , a sender on the engine block and the fan motor that all need to be checked. One of them must be bad.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||06-11-2001||06:07 PM||||Yes, check the fuse. And the relay is located by the driver's side headlight. It may need to be replaced.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000003||84 2in1||06-11-2001||06:18 PM||||where can I get the relay?||||reg||1
Z||000004||84 2in1||06-11-2001||06:39 PM||||Also where is the fuse? In the fuse block?||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||06-11-2001||09:47 PM||||You can pick up a new relay at your local parts store. And the fan relay fuse is the #4 fuse in the fuse block. Looking straight at the fuse block, it's in the top right. It's a yellow 20 amp fuse.||||reg||1
Z||000006||84 2in1||06-11-2001||10:27 PM||||Well Auto zone and advance neither one has the relay for the heavy duty cooling system with factory air. Actually took the relay into each store and tried to cross reference it to their stock # and no luck . will try again at Napa and Carquest tomorrow. thanx for the help so far . If any one has any more ideas where I can locate one please let me know . one last thing the Hanes manual mentioned that there is a fusible link in the system . Is there and if there is where is it?-B-<P>------------------<BR>If it works DON"T FIX IT!||||reg||8
Z||000007||DecadenceR||06-11-2001||10:51 PM||||84, I'm having the same problem with my 84SE.<BR>So far I replaced the sending switch, the fuse, and the relay.<BR>The relay is available at The Fiero Store for about $60.50, part no 60131.<BR>Hope you have better luck than I did!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||maryjane||06-12-2001||01:07 AM||||NAPA told me they can order this relay but did't carry it in stock. around $65. I found one in a junkyard. so far it's working ok.<BR>You should be able to check for voltage at the relay with the a/c on and also again with the sending switch jumped. The Haynes manual wiring diagram shows a red wire that is hot at all times, a dark green/wht wire coming from the coolant temp switch.it energizes the low speed part of the fan relay.a lightgreen/blk wire energizes the high speed part. The red (hot at all times) wire is shown with a fusible link but I don't know where it is located. If voltage is available at the green/wht,grn/blk wires, that means the temp switch is good(asumming there is no break in the circuit.). The Haynes wiring diagrams are not always accurate so take all this for what it's worth. I've seen a thread somewhere on exactly how to troubleshoot the fan and relay. Have you tried a search? Turn the key to on, have someone turn the a/c on while you look at the relay or put your hand on it if the cover is on. you should be able to feel ,hear or see it when it snaps on. Mine got water in it once and when I removed the cover, it was corroded. I cleaned the contacts,dried it out and it worked for about a year.My apologies if you have already tried all this.<BR>Don<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 06-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||maryjane||06-12-2001||01:47 AM||||I have another diagram I downloaded that shows the fusible link at or near the battery junction block, but I don't remember what year or model this diagram is for. If you find it, let us know where it is. You might try removing the hot at all times wire, running a hot wire from the battery to this terminal and see if the fan will come on with the a/c on. good luck<BR>Don||||reg||1
