Z||000011||DecadenceR||06-12-2001||11:04 PM||||You're in the same boat I am bro...<BR>I'll make sure I keep you updated on anmything I find too.||||reg||1
Z||000012||johnt671||06-13-2001||05:59 PM||||I had the same problem a while back, and gave up on making the fan work properly so I installed a switch so I can turn it off and on when I want to.||||reg||1
Z||000013||theogre||06-13-2001||07:22 PM||||Read the fan article in my cave... It might help.<P>Unplug the fan power connector near it's frame. Check for resistance between the 2 hot leads. There should be a couple ohms there. If there is no resistance there try between the low speed wire and the ground lead. If still nothing then the risistor is open and you'll have to bypass it.||||reg||1
